  "id": "Compound::DB00881 - Gene::6564",
  "verbalization": "Quinapril, a clinically used antihypertensive drug, is shown to bind to Slc15a2, a protein involved in transport processes across cellular membranes. The evidence suggests that Slc15a2 participates in various transport activities, including proton-dependent peptide transport and proton/oligonucleotide cotransport. These mechanisms are all part of a broader category of transmembrane transporters that facilitate the movement of molecules across cell membranes, often in a coupled or symport manner. The integration of these pathways implies that Quinapril may influence the function of Slc15a1 through its interaction with Slc15a2, potentially modulating the transport of peptides or nucleic acids across cellular membranes. The observed scores indicate a consistent and significant relationship between Quinapril and Slc15a1, suggesting a plausible functional link that warrants further experimental validation.",
